title: Hoi An's lantern boat — $6 or $20? (2026)
format: story
charstyle: nutshell
voice: af_heart
music: night
score: night@1 wonder@2 upbeat@3 comedy@4 wonder@5 emotional@6 night@7 tension@9 upbeat@10
sources: Vietadvisor "Is the Hoi An Lantern Boat Ride Really Worth It?" Sep 2026 (170,000 VND per boat for 1–3, 220,000 for 4–5; ~20 min; ~4pm–9:30pm; lanterns 5–15k extra; online listings ~$7.85–10.42 per person; full moon on the 14th lunar day, street lights off; Oct–Nov floods stop boats; 6–7pm busiest, 8:30 shorter queue; Ancient Town ticket 120k separate); trvlogue.com Hoi An lantern boat guide, Sep 2026 (170k / 220k per boat, ~20 min, 4–9:30pm, lanterns ~10k); danangfantasticity.com Ancient Town tickets 2026 (80k and 120k tickets, valid up to 3 days). Checked Oct 2026.
// ANGLE   The same 20-minute boat costs about $6.50 at the booth and $16–21 online — because one sells per boat, the other per person.
// CAMERA  macro lantern ignition → aerial river map → isometric booth → POV phone + balance scale → macro water release →
//         water-level moonrise → riverfront dusk clock → macro ticket punch → flood cutaway → turning lantern save card → aerial bay.
// RULE    v11: no mascot, no standing cast. Hands, boats, lanterns, prices and light are the actors.
// SOUND   match strike + fire whoosh, river bed, coins and counter, scale clank, splash, switches clicking off, chimes, rain.
// VIRAL   "$6 or $20?" at 1.3 s; the per-boat twist; the 3× scale; save card; open loop to Phu Quoc.

// 0:00 MACRO: a match flares and lights the candle inside a red silk lantern, the glow blooms — WHIP OUT to an AERIAL of the
//      river at night, boats and floating lanterns drifting; "$6 OR $20?" slams; "SAME BOAT. SAME RIVER."
# vis kind=ha act=hook
Twenty minutes on a lantern boat in Hoi An.
Some people pay six dollars. Some pay twenty.
Same boat. Same river.
// 0:10 MATCH to the aerial map turning slowly: two bridges, a dotted route drawn by a boat; "20 MIN" lands.
# vis kind=ha act=river trans=ripple tc=.5,.5
The boats row the Hoai River, between the An Hoi and Cam Nam bridges.
About twenty minutes, from four in the afternoon until half past nine.
// 0:20 BLOBS to an ISOMETRIC kiosk on the bank: the board fills line by line, a hand slides coins, a ticket pops up.
# vis kind=ha act=booth trans=blobs
At the riverside booths, the standard price is per boat.
One to three people: one hundred and seventy thousand dong.
Four or five: two hundred and twenty thousand.
// 0:32 WHIP to a POV phone: a listing priced per person, a thumb taps +1 → $16–21; the phone swings away, a brass scale drops in
//      and tips: online heavy, booth light; "3× MORE".
# vis kind=ha act=phone trans=whip
Online, the same ride is usually sold per person: eight to ten dollars each.
For two people, that's sixteen to twenty-one dollars.
At the booth, about six and a half.
// 0:45 LIQUID into a water-level MACRO: a pole lowers a lotus lantern, ripples ring out, it drifts away; "NOT INCLUDED" → "5–15K".
# vis kind=ha act=release trans=liquid tcol=#1a1a5a
The floating lanterns aren't included.
Sellers on the bank charge five to fifteen thousand each.
// 0:52 BLOOM up into a moonrise from the water: street lights click off one by one, the river fills with lanterns.
# vis kind=ha act=moon trans=bloom tc=.62,.3 tcol=#fff2c8
On the fourteenth day of every lunar month, the town switches the street lights off.
The river fills with lanterns, and the queues get long.
// 1:03 SLICES to the riverfront at dusk: a tower clock runs from six to half past eight, the sky goes indigo, the queue shrinks.
# vis kind=ha act=clock trans=slices
Six to seven is the prettiest hour, and the busiest.
Come at half past eight for a short queue.
// 1:11 DROP onto a MACRO ticket: a punch bites a hole; "SEPARATE".
# vis kind=ha act=ticket trans=drop
The Ancient Town ticket isn't part of it either.
That's another one hundred and twenty thousand, valid for up to three days.
// 1:19 SPIN into a rainy CUTAWAY of the river steps: the water climbs, tied boats bob, a gauge rises; "OCT – NOV / NO BOATS".
# vis kind=ha act=flood trans=spin
And in October and November, floods can stop the boats with no warning.
// 1:25 ZOOM THROUGH the rain into a great hexagonal lantern that turns one lit panel per rule.
# vis kind=ha act=rules trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.5
So: buy at the booth.
Pay per boat, not per person.
And keep some cash for a lantern.
// 1:34 MATCH the lantern glow to sun on water: an AERIAL of a turquoise bay — "NEXT: PHU QUOC".
# vis kind=ha act=tease trans=match tc=.5,.5
Next time: Phu Quoc.
